retrieved for Kuwait addressing joint controller arrangements. Without target text, each slot is assessed as uncovered. Relevant provisions may exist elsewhere in Kuwaiti law but were not available here.", "label": "C5", "ru_id": "RU-215", "gdpr_article": 26, "jurisdiction": "KWT", "ablation": "full", "direction": null, "sufficiency_curve": [{"round": 1, "n_queries": 1, "new": 0, "total": 0}], "sufficiency_met": false, "slot_completeness": 1.0, "rule_vs_holistic_agree": false, "n_revisions": 0, "objections": [], "n_candidates": 0, "candidate_ids": [], "n_llm_calls": 2, "latency_s": 95.13, "temperature": 0.7, "seed": 20260801, "id": "f57f5323a3e36938902f", "condition": "stability", "rep": 0}
{"candidates_selected": [], "candidates_excluded": [{"id": "674524dee00496cb5de7", "reason": "Article 7 imposes general obligations on a single controller to implement technical/organizational measures and keep records; it does not mention multiple controllers, joint control, or a transparent arrangement allocating responsibilities among controllers."}, {"id": "e05de90f481c9410c6e0", "reason": "Article 9 allocates breach-notification duties between controller and processor, not among multiple controllers; it contains no duty for joint controllers to determine respective responsibilities by arrangement."}, {"id": "9630e6d967b64e07d339", "reason": "Article 10 requires appointing a DPO by the controller or processor and notifying contact details; it does not address allocation of compliance responsibilities between multiple controllers."}, {"id": "717a67a0d311f88c5fd9", "reason": "Article 13 sets the controller’s information duties to the data subject but does not contemplate joint controllers or require an inter-controller arrangement to apportion those duties."}, {"id": "dec351a1e477287e3b22", "reason": "Article 19 requires a controller to provide clear contact methods for data subjects; it does not regulate relationships or responsibility allocation among multiple controllers."}, {"id": "34f7595acb9df257ef5e", "reason": "Article 11 defines DPO roles and powers; it does not create or require a joint-controller arrangement."}, {"id": "9c38ab11b550755816f5", "reason": "Article 12 sets duties of the controller/processor toward the DPO; it does not govern allocation of responsibilities between multiple controllers."}, {"id": "80f95c322bb3204c7f65", "reason": "Article 6 on consent conditions is unrelated to joint-controller arrangements."}, {"id": "743bfdd72ed773ff5ba9", "reason": "Article 2 on scope of application contains no rules about joint controllers or arrangements."}, {"id": "c34922f387019af45e42", "reason": "Article 18 addresses automated decision-making rights; it does not establish joint-controller responsibility allocation."}, {"id": "0897840c01b58a706cd5", "reason": "Article 26 concerns administrative sanctions; it does not address joint-controller arrangements."}, {"id": "1f0de28c69e3ad65d235", "reason": "Article 27 concerns delegation of supervisory powers; it does not address joint-controller arrangements."}], "target_frame": {"addressee": {"span": null, "article": null}, "modality": {"span": null, "article": null}, "action": {"span": null, "article": null}, "scope": {"span": null, "article": null}, "condition": {"span": null, "article": null}, "exception": {"span": null, "article": null}, "temporal": {"span": null, "article": null}, "consequence": {"span": null, "article": null}}, "slot_verdicts": [{"slot": "addressee", "gdpr": "joint controllers", "target": null, "basis": "absent", "verdict": "uncovered", "citation": null}, {"slot": "modality", "gdpr": "obligation", "target": null, "basis": "absent", "verdict": "uncovered", "citation": null}, {"slot": "action", "gdpr": "determine their respective responsibilities for compliance by means of an arrangement, in a transparent manner", "target": null, "basis": "absent", "verdict": "uncovered", "citation": null}, {"slot": "scope", "gdpr": "responsibilities for compliance, particularly on data subject rights and duties to provide information (Arts. 13 and 14)", "target": null, "basis": "absent", "verdict": "uncovered", "citation": null}, {"slot": "condition", "gdpr": "None", "target": null, "basis": "absent", "verdict": "covered", "citation": null}, {"slot": "exception", "gdpr": "unless and insofar as law determines those responsibilities", "target": null, "basis": "absent", "verdict": "uncovered", "citation": null}, {"slot": "temporal", "gdpr": "None", "target": null, "basis": "absent", "verdict": "covered", "citation": null}, {"slot": "consequence", "gdpr": "None", "target": null, "basis": "absent", "verdict": "covered", "citation": null}], "holistic_label": "uncovered", "confidence": 0.68, "reasoning_note": "The UAE PDPL provisions provided impose duties on a controller and on a processor, but they do not establish or require a transparent inter-controller arrangement to apportion compliance responsibilities. Articles cited by the reviewer reflect general or controller–processor allocations, not joint-controller arrangements. No distributed wording across the articles amounts to the GDPR Art. 26 duty.", "label": "C5", "ru_id": "RU-215", "gdpr_article": 26, "jurisdiction": "UAE", "ablation": "full", "direction": null, "sufficiency_curve": [{"round": 1, "n_queries": 1, "new": 11, "total": 11}, {"round": 2, "n_queries": 4, "new": 7, "total": 18}, {"round": 3, "n_queries": 4, "new": 0, "total": 18}], "sufficiency_met": true, "slot_completeness": 1.0, "rule_vs_holistic_agree": false, "n_revisions": 4, "objections": [{"verdict": "revise", "objection": "The provisions provided suggest that controllers and processors have a responsibility to work together to ensure compliance with the regulation, which could be seen as a counterpart to the GDPR requirement.", "counter_evidence": [{"id": "9c38ab11b550755816f5", "span": "المادة (12) واجبات المتحكم والمعالج تجاه مسؤول حماية البيانات", "why": "This article outlines the obligations of the controller and processor towards the data protection officer, which implies that they have a responsibility to work together to ensure compliance with the regulation."}, {"id": "dec351a1e477287e3b22", "span": "المادة (19) طرق التواصل مع المتحكم", "why": "This article discusses the ways in which data subjects can communicate with controllers, which implies that controllers have a responsibility to ensure that data subjects can exercise their rights."}, {"id": "34f7595acb9df257ef5e", "span": "المادة (11) أدوار مسؤول حماية البيانات", "why": "This article outlines the roles of the data protection officer, which includes ensuring that controllers and processors are compliant with the regulation."}], "confidence": 0.8}, {"verdict": "revise", "objection": "Potential for shared responsibilities among controllers or processors under different terminology or across several provisions", "counter_evidence": [{"id": "7", "span": "اتخاذ الإجراءات والتدابير التقنية والتنظيمية الملائمة", "why": "Implies shared responsibilities in data protection"}, {"id": "9", "span": "الإبلاغ عن انتهاك البيانات الشخصية", "why": "Suggests shared responsibilities in breach notification"}, {"id": "10", "span": "تعيين مسؤول لحماية البيانات", "why": "Implies responsibility sharing among controllers or processors"}], "confidence": 0.7}], "n_candidates": 12, "candidate_ids": ["9c38ab11b550755816f5", "dec351a1e477287e3b22", "34f7595acb9df257ef5e", "80f95c322bb3204c7f65", "743bfdd72ed773ff5ba9", "9630e6d967b64e07d339", "1f0de28c69e3ad65d235", "c34922f387019af45e42", "717a67a0d311f88c5fd9", "674524dee00496cb5de7", "e05de90f481c9410c6e0", "0897840c01b58a706cd5"], "n_llm_calls": 7, "latency_s": 535.2, "temperature": 0.7, "seed": 20260801, "id": "84377560ecb3d7cfce9d", "condition": "stability", "rep": 0}
{"candidates_selected": ["c511c9bf7779067e64f4"], "candidates_excluded": [{"id": "f8c6dae3f69fbe207307", "reason": "Addresses disclosure exceptions generally; does not regulate processing of criminal-conviction/offence data nor set Article 6(1)-like conditions or exceptions."}, {"id": "6f4fee23b0aedf942410", "reason": "Concerns restrictions on the right of access; not about processing of criminal-conviction/offence data."}, {"id": "952167864cc3b0d724c1", "reason": "Regulates withdrawal of consent; not specific to criminal-conviction/offence data nor to prohibitions/exceptions thereof."}, {"id": "c95a0b593cc554df0eae", "reason": "Record-keeping obligations; unrelated to prohibiting or authorizing processing of criminal-conviction/offence data."}, {"id": "ea8306cd18f9261f6413", "reason": "Transparency at collection; does not create a prohibition or exception specific to criminal-conviction/offence data."}, {"id": "a79606d0fb564d3b2b5d", "reason": "Breach notification; not about lawful bases or prohibitions for processing criminal-conviction/offence data."}, {"id": "21847c9e87d6df45a9a7", "reason": "Data quality obligations; no rule targeting criminal-conviction/offence data."}, {"id": "90da7bc2380e8f3f2fb8", "reason": "Response timelines for data subject requests; not about the RU’s prohibition/exception framework."}, {"id": "8394f801a0a97e521f68", "reason": "DPO appointment; not about processing of criminal-conviction/offence data."}, {"id": "557230873031d6e5cb2c", "reason": "Marketing with personal data (excluding sensitive data); not a prohibition on criminal-conviction/offence data."}, {"id": "ba8aef540689169aa848", "reason": "Indirect collection conditions and anonymization; not about criminal-conviction/offence data."}], "target_frame": {"addressee": {"span": "جهة التحكم", "article": "Article 10 (c511c9bf7779067e64f4)"}, "modality": {"span": null, "article": null}, "action": {"span": null, "article": null}, "scope": {"span": null, "article": null}, "condition": 