d codes as Art. 46(2)(e) transfer safeguards. Because no UAE text addresses codes of conduct, approval/general validity, or their use as transfer safeguards, the requirement is textually uncovered.", "label": "C5", "ru_id": "RU-487", "gdpr_article": 40, "jurisdiction": "UAE", "ablation": "full", "direction": null, "sufficiency_curve": [{"round": 1, "n_queries": 1, "new": 12, "total": 12}, {"round": 2, "n_queries": 4, "new": 6, "total": 18}, {"round": 3, "n_queries": 4, "new": 3, "total": 21}], "sufficiency_met": true, "slot_completeness": 1.0, "rule_vs_holistic_agree": false, "n_revisions": 4, "objections": [{"verdict": "revise", "objection": "Potential indirect support for data protection and security measures in UAE legislation", "counter_evidence": [{"id": "7", "span": "المادة (7) الالتزامات العامة للمتحكم", "why": "Implies a framework for protecting personal data"}, {"id": "20", "span": "المادة (20) أمن معلومات البيانات الشخصية", "why": "Mandates appropriate technical and organizational measures for data security"}, {"id": "11", "span": "المادة (11) أدوار مسؤول حماية البيانات", "why": "Suggests a structured approach to ensuring data protection compliance"}], "confidence": 0.7}, {"verdict": "revise", "objection": "The UAE has data protection regulations that could provide a foundation for safeguards in international data transfers, even if not directly equivalent to GDPR's codes of conduct.", "counter_evidence": [{"id": "7", "span": "المادة (7) الالتزامات العامة للمتحكم", "why": "Outlines general obligations for data protection, including appropriate technical and organizational measures."}, {"id": "20", "span": "المادة (20) أمن معلومات البيانات الشخصية", "why": "Discusses security measures for personal data, indicating a focus on protecting data during processing."}, {"id": "11", "span": "المادة (11) أدوار مسؤول حماية البيانات", "why": "Introduces the role of a data protection officer, suggesting a structured approach to ensuring data protection compliance."}], 