, "holistic_label": "uncovered", "confidence": 0.62, "reasoning_note": "Articles 3 and 8 set general privacy rights and controller obligations, but they do not grant a permission to enact more specific rules for processing employees’ personal data in the employment context, nor do they mention collective agreements. No cited provision addresses employment-specific processing or empowers such sectoral rulemaking.", "label": "C5", "ru_id": "RU-960", "gdpr_article": 88, "jurisdiction": "QAT", "ablation": "full", "direction": null, "sufficiency_curve": [{"round": 1, "n_queries": 1, "new": 6, "total": 6}, {"round": 2, "n_queries": 4, "new": 3, "total": 9}, {"round": 3, "n_queries": 4, "new": 2, "total": 11}], "sufficiency_met": false, "slot_completeness": 1.0, "rule_vs_holistic_agree": false, "n_revisions": 4, "objections": [{"verdict": "revise", "objection": "Counterpart exists under different terminology", "counter_evidence": [{"id": "a200ece03fd0ba143354", "span": "تُحدد، بقرار من الوزير، الضوابط والإجراءات المتعلقة بممارسة الأفراد للحقوق المنصوص عليها في المادتين السابقتين.", "why": "This article allows the Minister to determine controls and procedures for the exercise of rights, which could include more specific rules for the protection of rights and freedoms in respect of the processing of employees' personal data in the employment context."}], "confidence": 0.8}, {"verdict": "revise", "objection": "The Qatari law has provisions that provide a counterpart to the GDPR requirement, such as Article 3 and Article 8.", "counter_evidence": [{"id": "2bcce9feda2fcb9d35fe", "span": "لكل فرد الحق في حماية خصوصية بياناته الشخصية", "why": "This provision recognizes the right to protect personal data, which is a counterpart to the GDPR requirement."}, {"id": "a200ece03fd0ba143354", "span": "يتعين على المراقب الالتزام بما يلي: 1- معالجة البيانات الشخصية بأمانة ومشروعية", "why": "This provision requires the controller to process personal data with integrity and legitimacy, which 